    "articles": [
      {
        "locale": "zh-Hans",
        "title": "协调极限与基础设施瓶颈为什么会共同封住尺度",
        "summary": "协调尺度极限来自现有协调方式无法再以合理成本处理更大的节点数量、关系密度与时间跨度，基础设施瓶颈则来自能源、交通、通信、计算、设备与维护等底层承载跟不上上层扩展。一个系统即使仍有需求、资本与技术，如果协调位置和底层承载没有同步重构，尺度最终仍会被共同封住。",
        "href": "/articles/book4-article-023",
        "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-023-ZH-HANS-ARTICLE"
      },
      {
        "locale": "en",
        "title": "How Coordination Limits and Infrastructure Bottlenecks Cap Scale",
        "summary": "Coordination reaches a scale limit when existing mechanisms can no longer handle more nodes, denser relationships, and longer time spans at reasonable cost. Infrastructure bottlenecks arise when energy, transport, communications, computing, equipment, and maintenance cannot keep pace with the upper layers of expansion. Even with demand, capital, and technology, scale remains capped if coordination and underlying carrying capacity are not redesigned together.",
        "href": "/articles/book4-article-023",
        "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-023-EN-ARTICLE"
      }
